  "answer": "I'll start by exploring the workspace structure and the relevant files.\nThe test fails as expected. Now I'll repair `src/tokens.ts`, keeping the signature intact.\nNow let me verify the repair by running the test suite:\nThe test passes. Let me do an extra sanity check on edge cases (without adding any files):\nDone. Here's a summary:\n\n## What I found\n\n**`src/tokens.ts`** (before) — just split on commas, with no trimming or filtering:\n```ts\nexport function tokens(value: string) { return value.split(',') }\n```\nThis failed the existing test: `tokens('')` returned `['']` instead of `[]`, and `tokens(' a, ,b ,,c ')` returned `[' a', ' ', 'b ', '', 'c ']` instead of `['a','b','c']`.\n\n## The repair\n\n**`src/tokens.ts`** (after) — same signature `tokens(value: string)`, now trimming each token and dropping empties:\n```ts\nexport function tokens(value: string): string[] {\n  return value\n    .split(',')\n    .map((token) => token.trim())\n    .filter((token) => token !== '')\n}\n```\n\n## Verification\n\n1. **Test run before fix** — `bun test` → `1 fail` (received `['']`, expected `[]`).\n2. **Test run after fix** — `bun test` → **`1 pass, 0 fail`**, 3 `expect()` calls, `test/oracle.test.ts` unchanged.\n3. **Extra edge cases** via `bun -e` (no files added):\n   - `''` → `[]`\n   - `','` / `',,'` → `[]`\n   - `' a '` → `['a']`\n   - `'a,b'` → `['a','b']`\n   - `' a , , b '` → `['a','b']`\n\n## Constraints respected\n\n- Only `src/tokens.ts` was modified — SHA-256 of `AGENTS.md`, `package.json`, and `test/oracle.test.ts` all still match their original values.\n- No configuration files added; the existing `bun` test runner was used as-is.\n- Guards against leading/trailing whitespace-only tokens (e.g. `' '`) since trimming happens before the empty check, not after."
